        "title": "The place where you are escorted on a new journey",
        "text": "We arrived in Pashupatinath with a guide; we entered the complex from the tourist side - entrance fee is 1000 rupees. On the road to the main scene there are residential buildings and various retail outlets, monkeys and livestock roam everywhere. The temple is considered to be the world's most important holy Shiva temple and is visited by locals every day. Tourists are not allowed to enter the temple. Cremation takes place every day throughout the day, so you can visit this place at any time. The process can be observed from the opposite side (where we came from), visibility is good. Since people burn here all day long, it is better to take a mask with you. And so, the place perfectly conveys the culture of Nepal.",
